      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "Bile-stained vomiting in a newborn is an obstruction distal to the ampulla of Vater. A normal or abnormal upper GI contrast study showing a twisted or corkscrew duodenum is most consistent with midgut volvulus, which is a surgical emergency.",
